course: dictionary
lesson: 8051
title: Practice before the show
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A rehearsal is a practice before the real performance. The clues are in the words around it. «Then come weeks of rehearsals: learning lines out loud, learning where to stand, and practising the bows at the end.» Those are all things you do when you practise a play, so a rehearsal must be a practice.
explain: Rehearsals happen for plays, concerts, dances and shows. A rehearsal can also be any practice for an important event, like a fire drill or practising a speech. A dress rehearsal is the last full practice, done in costume as if it were real. The word «dress» is your clue: you wear the costume.
explain: «The conductor keeps dozens of players together, deciding how fast, loud and gentle each part is, mostly in rehearsals.» The word mostly tells you that the big decisions are made during practice, not on the night. When you meet a new word, swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: A rehearsal is a practice for a performance, such as a play, a concert or a show.
fact: A dress rehearsal is the last full practice, done in costume as if it were real.
fact: A rehearsal can be any practice for an important event, like a fire drill or practising a speech.
fact: «A band cannot rehearse full songs if people do not turn up.» Rehearsals need people to practise together.
exercise: «Then come weeks of rehearsals: learning lines out loud, learning where to stand.» What is a rehearsal? | A costume worn on the night | *A practice before the real performance | A ticket for the audience | A loud song played at the end
exercise: Mia says a dress rehearsal is the same as any normal rehearsal. What is the difference? | *A dress rehearsal is the last full practice, done in costume as if it were real | A dress rehearsal is for people who sew clothes | A dress rehearsal happens after the show
exercise: «The conductor keeps dozens of players together, mostly in rehearsals.» Find and copy the word that tells you where the conductor makes most decisions. | concert | players | *rehearsals | baton
test: Which one is a rehearsal? | *Practising a speech before the school assembly | Reading a book at bedtime | Eating lunch early in the hall | Sitting in the front row of a concert
test: The play is «in rehearsal» this week. What does that mean? | It has finished and been filmed | It is a sleepy afternoon | It is cancelled until next year | *It is being practised before the real show
exam: «The band cannot rehearse full songs if people do not turn up.» Why do the band members need to turn up? | So they can sell tickets early | *So they can practise full songs together | So the sound is louder for the neighbours | So they can buy new instruments
